# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: autolisp-cli-tests-missing — test-op references a non-existent test system
#+STATUS: DONE
#+PRIORITY: P3
#+TYPE: infra
#+DEPENDS: -
#+BRANCH: fix-autolisp-cli-tests-missing

* Resolution (2026-08-03, clautolisp 1.7.14)

Registered the missing =clautolisp/autolisp-cli/tests= system so the
=clautolisp/autolisp-cli= test-op resolves, and gave the CLI layer a
home for unit tests. Added:

- =clautolisp/autolisp-cli/tests/{package,test-harness,cli-launch-tests,run}.lisp=,
  mirroring =autolisp-builtins-core/tests= — same FiveAM shape,
  =run-all-tests= entry point, and a SETUP-MOCK-EVALUATION-CONTEXT
  fixture (runtime context backed by a fresh MockHost).
- the =(defsystem "clautolisp/autolisp-cli/tests" …)= in
  =clautolisp/clautolisp.asd=, and wired it into the aggregate
  =clautolisp/tests= (depends-on + the run-all-tests perform) so it runs
  under the default =make -C clautolisp test-sbcl=.

First tests, per the To-do below:
- APPLY-CLAUTOLISP-HOST-IDENTITY stamps PROGRAM / PRODUCT / VENDORNAME /
  PLATFORM / ACADVER (and leaves ACADVER untouched on a blank version);
- APPLY-TEMPPREFIX-DEFAULT resolution order (a stored registry value
  wins and is normalised; the empty-registry path still yields a
  non-empty, slash-terminated TEMPPREFIX) — driven against a hermetic
  temp-file registry store;
- the option value parsers (PARSE-HOST / PARSE-DIALECT / PARSE-TIMEOUT),
  including their CLI-USAGE-ERROR rejections.

Verification: =make -C clautolisp test-sbcl
TEST_SYSTEM=clautolisp/autolisp-cli/tests= → 25/25 checks pass.

* Symptom

clautolisp.asd wires a test-op for the CLI system:

    (asdf:defsystem "clautolisp/autolisp-cli"
      ...
      :in-order-to ((asdf:test-op
                     (asdf:test-op "clautolisp/autolisp-cli/tests"))))

but there is NO `(defsystem "clautolisp/autolisp-cli/tests" ...)` and no
`clautolisp/autolisp-cli/tests/` directory. So

    (asdf:test-system "clautolisp/autolisp-cli")

fails with a missing-system error, and there is nowhere to unit-test the
CLI layer (transmit bindings, apply-clautolisp-host-identity,
apply-launch-codepage-to-sysvars, apply-tempprefix-default, option
parsing).

* To do

- Add clautolisp/autolisp-cli/tests/{package,test-harness,run}.lisp and
  the defsystem, mirroring autolisp-builtins-core/tests (which already
  has setup-mock-evaluation-context — the exact fixture the CLI-launch
  functions need: a runtime context backed by a fresh MockHost).
- First tests to add: TEMPPREFIX resolution order (registry / TMPDIR /
  platform default + persistence), and the PROGRAM/VENDORNAME/ACADVER
  identity stamping.
- Until then, CLI-launch behaviour is only covered end-to-end by direct
  binary runs.
